      "text_helper": "Section 24.7.2 \"Time triggered communication mode\" in chapter 24 (Controller area network (bxCAN)), RM0008 Rev 21, page 662.",
      "section_content": "In this mode, the internal counter of the CAN hardware is activated and used to generate the\nTime Stamp value stored in the CAN_RDTxR/CAN_TDTxR registers, respectively (for Rx\nand Tx mailboxes). The internal counter is incremented each CAN bit time (refer to\nSection24.7.7). The internal counter is captured on the sample point of the Start Of Frame\nbit in both reception and transmission.",
